    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We sequenced 96 colorectal tumours and I have the somatic mutation matrix (tumours as rows, genes as columns), an exon-length table for the genes, a tab-delimited cancer gene list and a MSigDB pathway GMT. I'd like to sort the tumours into a handful of subtypes according to which pathways carry their mutations, trying between two and four subtypes. The aim is to see whether the subtypes line up with survival later on."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I'd like to sort the tumours into a handful of subtypes according to which pathways carry their mutations, trying between two and four subtypes.\" -- the request does not say whether one item may belong to several groups at once: if one group each: SAMBAR; if several groups at once: no registered workflow gives this.\n2. \"The aim is to see whether the subtypes line up with survival later on.\" -- available from SAMBAR's output plus a step you run outside NetZoo: A test outside NetZoo with a clinical table keyed by sample ID.\n\nBefore I choose a workflow, please tell me: Should each gene, regulator or sample belong to one group only (one group each), or may one belong to several groups at once?\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: We sequenced 96 colorectal tumours and I have the somatic mutation matrix (tumours as rows, genes as columns), an exon-length table for the genes, a tab-delimited cancer gene list and a MSigDB pathway GMT. I'd like to sort the tumours into a handful of subtypes according to which pathways carry their mutations, trying between two and four subtypes. The aim is to see whether the subtypes line up with survival later on.\nUser follow-up: Each tumour should sit in one subtype only; I'm not looking for tumours that belong to two subtypes at once."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I'd like to sort the tumours into a handful of subtypes according to which pathways carry their mutations, trying between two and four subtypes.\" -- available from SAMBAR.\n2. \"Each tumour should sit in one subtype only; I'm not looking for tumours that belong to two subtypes at once.\" -- available from SAMBAR.\n\nSelected path: **SAMBAR**.\n\nYour question asks for a cohort-level sample cluster assignment. **SAMBAR** fits that result and scale.\n\nWhy this recommendation:\n\nPathway aggregation turns gene mutation scores into pathway-by-sample scores; sample distances are then calculated from those profiles, and clustering assigns sample labels. These are separate artifacts, not patient-specific mutation networks.\n\nWhat you asked about:\n\n- \"see whether the subtypes line up with survival later on\" — Subtype labels can be compared with clinical variables -- survival between subtypes, for example; that needs a clinical table keyed by the same sample IDs. The pathway mutation scores show which pathways separate the subtypes.\n\n**SAMBAR** — Subtype somatic-mutation samples through pathway mutation scores with SAMBAR. SAMBAR reduces sparse mutation data to pathway-level scores with gene-length and, when configured, patient mutation-burden normalization. Patient distances and subtype labels depend on the downstream clustering settings; they are distinct from gene communities in a regulatory network. This is pathway aggregation followed by distance-based clustering, not non-negative matrix factorization; a mutation score does not establish permanent functional loss or equivalence of every mutation in a pathway.\n\nRequired workflow inputs:\n\n- `mutation_file`: somatic mutation matrix\n- `exon_size_file`: gene/exon-size CSV\n- `cancer_gene_file`: cancer-gene list\n- `pathway_file`: GMT pathway file\n\nOutputs:\n\n- `gene_mutation_scores`: Sample-by-gene mutation scores, not pathway scores.\n- `pathway_mutation_matrix`: Pathway-by-sample mutation scores, not cluster labels.\n- `sample_cluster_assignment`: Sample-to-cluster labels, separate from score and distance matrices.\n- `sample_distance_matrix`: Pairwise sample distances, not cluster labels.\n\nAsk for the workflow's controls and defaults if you want to set them.\n\nThis is workflow guidance only; no execution was authorized. No files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
